n-names></name></person-group> <article-title>Long-term experience with low dose methotrexate in rheumatoid arthritis.</article-title><source>Rheumatol Int</source><year>1993</year>;<volume>13</volume>:<fpage>103</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8235288</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b18"><label>18</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sander</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Herborn</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Bock</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Rau</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>Prospective six year follow up of patients withdrawn from a randomised study comparing parenteral gold salt and methotrexate.</article-title><source>Ann Rheum Dis</source><year>1999</year>;<volume>58</volume>:<fpage>281</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10225812</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b19"><label>19</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Menninger</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Herborn</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Sander</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Blechschmidt</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Rau</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>A 36 month comparative trial of methotrexate and gold sodium thiomalate in the treatment of early active and erosive rheumatoid arthritis.</article-title><source>Br J Rheumatol</source><year>1998</year>;<volume>37</volume>:<fpage>1060</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9825744</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b20"><label>20</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nagashima</surname